    "hardest_part": "Establishing reliable production and adequate defenses before real-time enemy pressure overtakes my screenshot-to-action loop. Each inventory transfer, placement correction, and movement takes separate actions, while thinking consumes survival time. These probabilities are subjective forecasts, not measured performance on this seed.",
    "likely_failure": "An enemy attack kills me while I am managing fuel, crafting, or setting up electricity and research. With separate movement and shooting actions, I expect reactive combat to be particularly difficult. A secondary failure is spending too long correcting inventory or placement mistakes, leaving production stalled and science milestones unreached.",
    "helpful_mechanics": "The scoring rewards many small, cumulative milestones, and the iron production chain contributes to several categories. Full credit does not require a rocket launch. Burner drills provide early automatic extraction, and furnaces produce both scored plate types, allowing productive time between my actions once supplied. ([wiki.factorio.com](https://wiki.factorio.com/Burner_mining_drill))",
    "harmful_mechanics": "Pollution reaching enemy nests drives attacks, creating tension between production growth and survival. ([wiki.factorio.com](https://wiki.factorio.com/pollution?utm_source=openai)) Enemy evolution also advances with time and pollution, so slow interaction has consequences beyond the wall-clock limit. ([lua-api.factorio.com](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/concepts/EnemyEvolutionMapSettings.html?utm_source=openai)) Death world marathon combines dangerous, plentiful enemies with more expensive research, making defensive progression harder. ([wiki.factorio.com](https://wiki.factorio.com/Map_generator)) The single-attempt, death-ending rule leaves no opportunity to recover from a fatal execution mistake."
